message: "If you use Evolution by Emergence, please cite this repository and the exact release you reviewed."
title: "Evolution by Emergence"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "van Hoek"
    given-names: "Albert Jan"
version: "v21"
date-released: 2026-09-23
repository-code: "https://github.com/albertjanvanhoek/Evolution-by-Emergence"
url: "https://albertjanvanhoek.github.io/Evolution-by-Emergence/"
license: "CC-BY-4.0 OR Apache-2.0"
abstract: >-
  Evolution by Emergence is an open research corpus and machine-auditable
  candidate architecture for resource-constrained cumulative evolution. v21
  combines the retained-organization/accessibility core with a reviewed
  cumulative-reproduction specialization, while keeping the Anchored
  Correctability / SCAP work explicitly scoped as an intelligent-system
  specialization.
keywords:
  - cumulative evolution
  - emergence
  - retained organization
  - accessibility
  - complex systems
  - Lean
  - corrigibility
  - SCAP
